Using <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> camera features in the Home app will require an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/icloud/">iCloud</a>+ plan starting at 2TB, according to Apple. Apple shared the detail in its notes for the third <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a> beta that was released today.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/iOS-26-Home-Glass-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1034992" /><br/>
In <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-27/">iPadOS 27</a>, and macOS 27 Golden Gate, the Home app is able to generate written summaries for motion alerts from <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/homekit-secure-video/">HomeKit Secure Video</a> cameras. It's also able to group footage from separate cameras for an overview of activity and pull out noteworthy recordings, plus it supports natural language search.<br/>
<br/>
Apple said at WWDC that some &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; features would require an &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan, but Apple didn't specify which tier users would need to subscribe to. For the Home features, users will need the 2TB &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan or better. The 2TB plan includes 2TB of &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj; storage and it costs &#36;9.99 per month.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;HomeKit Secure Video&zwnj; cloud storage has always required a paid &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj; plan. The 50GB plan allows for one camera, while the 200GB plan supports up to five. The 2TB plan lets users add an unlimited number of &zwnj;HomeKit Secure Video&zwnj; cameras, and now it will also add the &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; Home feature set. <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/homekit/">HomeKit</a> video storage does not count against the storage limit of an &zwnj;iCloud&zwnj;+ plan, so the full 2TB stays available for photos and other data.<br/>
<br/>
